# Studio plan gate (Phase ①)

Prakrit only. When the user is **Akhil**, skip this gate unless he asks.
See [`docs/agents/AGENTS-prakrit.md`](docs/agents/AGENTS-prakrit.md) /
[`docs/agents/AGENTS-akhil.md`](docs/agents/AGENTS-akhil.md).

Full standard: [`docs/agents/lavish-plan-standard.md`](docs/agents/lavish-plan-standard.md).
This is the **one** plan pipeline — the older Lavish `workflow:plan` /
`lavish:poll` flow it replaces is retired, and `lane-workflow-v2.mdc` states
the same contract in short form.

**Every prompt from the captain becomes a lane plan in the PropLane studio
first.** A bug, an idea, a screenshot, one line in chat — plan it, open it,
iterate on it. **No product code** until the plan's status is `approved` (his
Approve button in the studio, or him typing **`build`** in that lane's pane).

**Do not file a Linear ticket for it.** The plan is the artifact. File a ticket
only when he explicitly asks ("file a ticket", "log this in Linear").

## When the captain describes work

```bash
node ~/proplane-mock-kit/tools/studio-plan.mjs new --lane <lane> --id <id> --title "<title>"
```

That writes `~/proplane-mock-kit/studio/plans/<lane>/<id>/plan.json` and the
sibling `plan.html`. Then **fill the scaffold** — it ships as a shell full of
`slot` placeholders and is not reviewable until you replace them.

Reply with: the lane's studio URL, one line on what the plan proposes, and
**"waiting on your edits"**. Do not implement yet.

## The plan quality bar

| Tab | Must contain |
| --- | --- |
| Overview | today (verified in the running app) → after, in/out of scope |
| **UI** | the screen **mocked** in PropLane tokens — before/after, desktop/mobile, empty + loading + error |
| Build | file-by-file table, data/contract changes, order of work |
| Decide | open questions as pickable options, each with cost/benefit |
| Risks & tests | failure modes; real seeded data + edges, never `/demo` as proof |

The plan is the spec: **what it shows is exactly what gets built**. If build
forces a departure, update `plan.html`, say what moved, and keep the same plan.

It must stay **semi-interactive and editable** — tabs, before/after and
desktop/mobile toggles, `contenteditable` sections with *Queue my edits*, and
decision forms that submit once. All of it reaches you through the lane's
studio inbox and nowhere else.

## Studio watch (mandatory — non-negotiable)

Captain feedback lives in the **studio**, not chat alone. A plan left open with
no watcher running is a dead page: he types into it and nothing happens.

**After writing or updating a plan:**

1. Start the watch as a **tracked background** task:
   `node ~/proplane-mock-kit/tools/studio-inbox.mjs --lane <lane> --wait`.
   One watcher per lane; two race for the same delivery.
2. Apply what came back by editing the **same** `plan.html`.
3. Reply inside the studio, where he wrote the note, then keep the watch open.

**Every later turn while the lane's `active.json` names this plan:** check the
watch is still live **before anything else**. If it was killed or timed out,
re-run it — queued feedback is never lost.

| Command | When |
| --- | --- |
| `studio-plan.mjs new --lane <lane> --id <id> --title "…"` | scaffold this lane's plan |
| `studio-inbox.mjs --lane <lane> --wait` | right after writing the plan, and every later turn |
| `studio-plan.mjs status --lane <lane>` | exits 0 once the plan is buildable |

**Never** tell the captain to annotate without a watcher running.
**Never** end a turn with a plan open and no watcher running.

## Do not

- Write feature code before the plan is buildable
- File a Linear ticket for the work (unless he asks)
- Ship a plan whose UI tab describes the screen instead of drawing it
- Leave `slot` placeholders in a plan you showed him
- Open a plan and end the turn without a watcher
- Start a second plan for the same lane while one is still active

Skip the gate only on an explicit **`skip plan`** (hotfix).
